{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "puppetdb",
  "description": "One fact walk plus one node page. Proves the structured Facter 4 facts are read (networking.interfaces per device, os.release.full, dmi.product.serial_number) and that the flat legacy fact names still work for a node that reports only those, that a bond and its slave device sharing one MAC are folded into a single interface rather than duplicated, that a node with no facts at all still imports on its certname, and that a node whose only address is 127.0.0.1 on the lo device yields an asset with NO interface -- Facter reports loopback on every node, so importing it would give the whole estate one shared address. A node with no certname and a non-object row are skipped.",
  "kwargs": {
    "url": "$BASE",
    "auth_token": "fixture-rbac-token",
    "page_size": "500",
    "fact_page_size": "2000"
  },
  "routes": [
    {
